  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_011 (multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, concat) achieves 0.536 acc, far exceeding image-only (0.208), confirming RNA is critical. The largest untested architectural axis is multiprofile with aggregation, which could capture inter-profile interactions and substantially improve accuracy. Question: Does adding multiprofile + transformer aggregation (while holding RNA encoder, image encoder, and fusion method constant) yield a meaningful gain over the singleprofile baseline? Why this experiment: config_001 is the most direct and powerful extension of the current best config, isolating the effect of multiprofile+transformer. Transformer aggregation is the most expressive option and likely to outperform avgpool. Expected cost is moderate (~1.0–1.5 GPU hours) since it uses resnet50 (not ViT-L) but adds transformer attention over multiple profiles—manageable given only 0.68 GPU hours used so far and 7 experiments remaining. If it succeeds, we can then escalate to ViT-L and scgpt in later experiments."
}

